@startuml activity-release-flow
!include elvira.iuml
' What: a GitHub release is the announcement; the site lists every release by itself and adds a hand-written post only for notable ones.
' Source: scripts/fetch-releases.mjs and .github/workflows/deploy.yml in this repository; evilflowers-actions README (2026-11-16)
' Scope: public repositories of the EvilFlowersCatalog organization. Left out: deployment to the STU servers.

title How a release reaches elvira.digital (2026-11)

|Repository|
start
:Maintainer updates the changelog\nand publishes a GitHub release\nwith tag X.Y.Z;
:CI builds what the tag ships\n(the Calibre plugin ZIP today;\nimage :X.Y.Z with evilflowers-actions);
|elvira.digital|
:Site rebuild\n(daily, on push, or by hand);
:Fetch releases of every public repository;
:List the release on /releases\nwith a link to its notes on GitHub;
if (notable release?) then (yes)
  :Write a post on /news:\nwhat changed for readers, librarians, operators;
else (no)
endif
stop

caption Release notes live on GitHub. The site links to them and does not copy them.
@enduml
